  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Now Playing",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"Now Playing\"**\n\nA live auction is the track that is playing right now. The item photo is the album cover, the countdown is the scrub bar, and the bid is the play button. One live item owns the screen: a large square artwork, its name and leader, a big tabular price, a progress timer, and one coral bid control. Everything else (upcoming, ended) sits below as horizontal album shelves that snap a whole card at a time.\n\nThe world is a deep plum night tinted by the artwork itself. The ambient backdrop pulls three colours from the active item's image and spreads them as slow-drifting, heavily dimmed blobs over the plum base, cross-fading in 900ms when the item changes. Text is warm cream, never grey. Coral is the single action voice. Depth comes from soft drop shadows under artwork and from one glass surface, the floating nav.\n\nDensity is low on the hero and medium on shelves and forms. The auction data (price, leader, bid count, remaining time) is the content; the music-player grammar is the frame, not a copy of any player's icons or layout.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Image-derived ambient colour field over a plum base, with a bottom-darkening scrim for contrast.",
      "One coral action per screen; coral also marks progress and the active tab.",
      "Manrope throughout; money and counts are weight 800 with tabular figures.",
      "Large rounded square artwork (20-28px corners) with deep soft shadows.",
      "1px cream hairlines at 8% for borders and dividers.",
      "Floating glass capsule nav (blur 30) as the only frosted chrome."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Coral is the only action colour. If something is coral, it is the bid, the primary CTA, progress, or the current location.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Cream Not Grey Rule",
        "body": "Text hues stay in the cream-to-mauve family; no neutral greys.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold Means Won Rule",
        "body": "Gold appears only where someone has won.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Money Rule",
        "body": "Every price, countdown and count uses tabular figures at weight 700-800.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Plain Label Rule",
        "body": "Section and field labels are sentence-case 13px/700 with no letter-spacing. No eyebrows.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Glass Is For Floating Rule",
        "body": "Backdrop blur (sigma 30) belongs to floating chrome (the nav capsule) and to chips laid over artwork. Content surfaces are tinted plum, not frosted.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Coral Halo Rule",
        "body": "A coloured glow is reserved for the coral action and urgent progress. Ordinary surfaces get neutral black shadows.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** let the active item's artwork tint the whole screen through AmbientBackdrop, and cross-fade it over 900ms when the item changes.",
      "**Do** keep exactly one coral action per screen and give it room.",
      "**Do** set every price, countdown and count in Manrope 800 with tabular figures.",
      "**Do** make the timer bar's length equal the true remaining fraction of the time window.",
      "**Do** use 1px cream hairlines (8%, 16% on glass) for borders and dividers.",
      "**Do** honour reduced motion: springs, beats, drift and slides collapse to instant changes.",
      "**Do** pad content by the nav inset so the floating nav never covers it."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use neutral greys for text; stay in cream, cream-soft and mauve.",
      "**Don't** put cream text on coral; use cta-ink.",
      "**Don't** use gold for anything except a win.",
      "**Don't** frost content cards; blur is for floating chrome and chips over artwork.",
      "**Don't** add eyebrow or kicker labels (small tracked uppercase lines above headings).",
      "**Don't** use hard-edged or sideways-offset shadows.",
      "**Don't** copy a music player's icons or layout; the auction data is the content."
    ]
  }
}